{
  "id": "noonan-syndrome",
  "term": "Noonan syndrome",
  "definition": "Noonan syndrome is a genetically varied disorder that affects physical development and commonly involves short stature, distinctive head and neck features, skeletal differences, heart problems, and hormonal or reproductive abnormalities. It can also involve some degree of intellectual disability and occurs in both males and females with a normal karyotype.",
